I may still never ascend, but I'm getting pretty
close now to being able to get _any_ character class
into Mine Town still at level 1 and ready to work
the protection racket (in the sense that I've done
it at least once for almost all of them, not that my
proportional success rate is very high for all of
them yet).  Some of them are still having problems
making it from there to the altar, but my now much
longer surviving pets are appreciating my extra
efforts on their behalf.  If I can make Mine Town
with two or three well buffed pets, I'm usually good
to go on the protection racket modulo some just horrid
misfortune (like all of my pets taking a simultaneous
and eventually suicidal dislike to the watch captain).

While I grant that there are character classes for
which the protection racket isn't all that good a
choice (knights in particular, whose pets have a
death-by-starvation wish), it is at least apparently
doable for them all.

xanthian.

